initial.quirel:
Use case: precise-object-edit.
Asset type: production game sprite sheet, targeted leg correction.
Input image 1 is the EDIT TARGET: eight original running sprites in a precise 4-column by 2-row grid of 384 x 384 pixel cells, total 1536 x 768. Keep this exact grid, canvas, scale, and original per-cell sprite placement.
Change ONLY the two legs below the pelvis in each cell to create a complete natural alternating 8-pose run cycle. Preserve the original head, torso, arms, weapons, cloak, tail, colors, texture, body proportions, hip position, and ALL pixels above the pelvis as closely as possible. This is NOT a new character design and NOT a replacement body. Keep leg lengths, muscular thickness, boot size, and claw shapes matching the originals. Both knees bend forward toward screen-right, heels fold backward toward screen-left, toes point right. Exactly two legs per pose. Far leg slightly darker and correctly behind the near leg. Full feet visible with no clipping. Both legs MUST change, exchange leading/supporting roles halfway through the cycle, and connect at their existing hip joints.
Eight poses read left to right across top row then bottom row. Anatomically track the same near leg and same far leg:
1 near leg reaches forward to contact, far leg trails behind at toe-off;
2 near leg supports under the hip, far heel lifts behind with knee bent;
3 near leg pushes backward, far knee swings forward with foot beneath knee;
4 near leg folds backward, far leg reaches forward preparing contact;
5 far leg contacts forward, near leg trails behind (opposite of pose 1);
6 far leg supports under the hip, near heel lifts behind (opposite of pose 2);
7 far leg pushes backward, near knee swings forward (opposite of pose 3);
8 far leg folds backward, near leg reaches forward ready to loop to pose 1.
Maintain original ground baseline at local cell y=368. Do not lengthen or shorten the legs, do not shrink bodies, do not straighten all legs, do not leave either foot fixed in all poses. No extra frames, no labels, no grid lines, no shadows, no scenery. Genuine transparent RGBA background, no opaque background or checkerboard. Return the edited 1536 x 768 sheet with only these eight original heroes.
Character: Quirel, the original lean golden-scaled heroine holding a double-ended staff. Preserve her lean original anatomy and dark boots.

